      "id": "frhkf5x",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Constitutional Articles Related to State Government"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The State Government executive consists of the Governor, Chief Minister, and Council of Ministers.",
        "State Legislature comprises the Governor and one or two houses depending on the state.",
        "The Legislative Assembly (Vidhan Sabha) serves as the popular, directly elected lower house.",
        "The Legislative Council (Vidhan Parishad) functions as the upper house in bicameral state legislatures.",
        "Constitutional Articles govern the powers, duties, and structures of all state administrative branches."
      ],
      "id": "aex1gyx"
    },
